<%# Figma frame 09. `config.sign_in_after_reset_password` is left at its default
    of true, so by the time this renders the user is signed in — which is why
    the body can promise it, and why this screen carries no back link.

    Devise's own behaviour is to redirect straight to the map. That is fine for
    a browser and useless on a phone, where the reset started in a mail app and
    the map is not what the user came for. This says the thing they need to
    know, and leaves going to the map as a choice. %>
<div class="auth-card">
  <div class="auth-badge auth-badge--success">
    <%= render "shared/auth_icon", name: :check_circle, size: 28 %>
  </div>

  <h1 class="auth-card__title">Password updated</h1>
  <p class="auth-card__subtitle">
    You're logged in to AirCasting and ready to go.
  </p>

  <%= link_to "Go to the map", root_path, class: "auth-button" %>
</div>
